+//! The seeded mutator: the half of a fuzzer that decides which inputs are tried.
+//!
+//! Step `lakelet/4.2-parser-fuzz`. A fuzzer without a mutator is a loop over one input; a fuzzer
+//! whose mutator is not reproducible is a test that passes on Tuesday and fails on Wednesday for
+//! reasons nobody can read. What this module owes the step's harness is the *search*: a stream of
+//! inputs, in an order a seed decides, that stays the same on every machine and in every process.
+//!
+//! This is the one part of the step's tools with no implementation: which mutations a format needs
+//! and how a generator is written are the step's work, and the contracts below are what the spec
+//! and the harness hold the work to.
+
+/// Walk `iterations` mutated inputs past `visit`, starting from `seed`.
+///
+/// Four rules are the walk's answer, and each one is a thing a mutator can get wrong:
+///
+/// * **the same seed walks the same inputs**, here and on any other machine: the generator is part
+///   of the answer, so it may not read the clock, the environment or an address of its own, and it
+///   may not ask a crate for entropy. A generator written out by hand is a few lines, and this
+///   project does not take a dependency it does not need;
+/// * **another seed walks somewhere else**, or the seed is decoration;
+/// * **every mutation kind this format has is in there** — truncation, byte flips, edits to the
+///   length field, inserted junk. They are not interchangeable: a walk that only truncates finds
+///   what a length is about and nothing else, and a walk that only flips bytes never hands anyone
+///   a frame that is cut short;
+/// * **the walk is not all rubbish**: it starts from frames `frame::decode` accepts and leaves
+///   some of them whole, because inputs the decoder *accepts* are how a refusal is told apart from
+///   a parser that has stopped working.
+///
+/// `visit` is handed one input at a time, and every input the walk produces has to reach it: the
+/// harness counts them, and a walk that keeps a promising input to itself has fuzzed nothing.
+pub fn walk(seed: u64, iterations: usize, visit: impl FnMut(&[u8])) {
+    let _ = (seed, iterations, visit);
+    todo!("step lakelet/4.2-parser-fuzz")
+}
